<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Caltex year net profit rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Caltex year net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>		(million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit	     43.65 vs  39.07</p>
<p>    Net profit		     57.70 vs  42.57</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	     14.0  vs  22.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Caltex Australia Ltd is a petroleum refiner and marketer and is 75 percent owned by  Caltex Petroleum Corp, which is owned 50 percent each by Chevron Corp and Texaco Inc.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		25 vs 22</p>
<p>    Sales				  91.76 vs 148.2</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay March 27</p>
<p>Reg March 18</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			 nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Tax			   credit 3.54 vs credit 3.71</p>
<p>NOTE: Net profit was after an extraordinary profit of A$10.55 million. Caltex's main business is its 50 percent stake in Australian Petroleum Pty Ltd (APPL), which followed a merger in 1995 of its petroleum retailing and refining operations with Ampol. Pioneer International Ltd hold the other half of APPL.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
